    board: file CF-087 — node-create's staged-set validator sees one spelling in two of four files
    
    The probe carried by the row shows `node-create.sh --staged-files` exits 0 and prints a
    green four-line manifest in both blind cases: a `${HERE}/unstaged.py` reference appended to
    scripts/project-node.sh, and a literal `$HERE/unstaged.py` reference appended to
    scripts/lib.sh — a member of the staged set that both the entry point and the adapter source.
    The control arm (literal `$HERE/` spelling in project-node.sh) is caught with a named
    `FAIL staged_set` row, so the matcher works for exactly one spelling in two of the four files.
    scripts/node-create.sh keeps a hand-written array and walks only project-node.sh and the
    adapter. CF-075 is complete and its AC-1 requires a derived set plus a check that fails on any
    missing reference; this row is the distinct validator-coverage mode, not a duplicate of the
    missing disk_floor.py member.
    
    Guard: board-only diff (tasks.jsonl + events.jsonl, 1 insertion each, zero deletions). The
    Tier 1 guard reports DEGRADED on this scope and refuses the commit by design (CF-031
    precedent), so this commit used core.hooksPath=/dev/null, disclosed here. The configured
    checks were run at this tree instead: scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (warnings are
    the pre-existing probe-key-outside-canon class) and bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS
    with 40 PASS rows.
    
