 {"id":"CF-086","title":"16 of 71 board rows embed absolute /home/kara paths, so a reader of this public repo cannot reproduce them — normalize to repo-relative or ~ and refuse new absolute host paths","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:25:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T16:25:42Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"cdbbf30ec4983b67ced60260135b79640cb0eb57623e6d3bac5427196f4acf75"},"reasoning":"Measured at 532e7b8 with git show HEAD:.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl | grep -c /home/kara = 16 of 71 rows (CF-009 CF-011 CF-012 CF-013 CF-037 CF-045 CF-052 CF-053 CF-055 CF-073 CF-074 CF-076 CF-084 CF-085 PERF-013 PERF-014). This repo is PUBLIC (gh repo view visibility=PUBLIC). Two costs: the rows leak the operator username, and any path the row cites as evidence is unusable off-host — the same reproducibility defect CF-084 files for CF-011/CF-013. Filed by the sync lane 2026-11-03 rather than rewritten in place, because 14 of the 16 rows predate this tick and rewriting evidence text is a separate, reviewable pass.","acceptance_criteria":"A repo check rejects a new or updated board row whose JSON contains an absolute /home/ or /tmp path unless the row names why the path cannot be repo-relative; the 16 rows measured at 532e7b8 are normalized (repo paths repo-relative, out-of-repo paths to ~ with the reason stated); verified by running the check over the committed board with zero findings and bash tests/selftest.sh exiting 0 with the case listed.","capability_tags":["board","public-repo","hygiene"]}
 {"id":"PERF-015","title":"P3 — a foreign commit landed mid-tick and added 6 gate assertions worth 0.345 s CPU (20% of the gate); the 'staged disk floor resolves' row alone is 0.151 s","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:28:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T16:28:24Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"a25aa570658d8771832d4dc2693a6cbf539b859e255e2c9738cc0bad03875276","evidence":[{"run_id":"code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-16-08-21","ts":"2026-11-03T16:28:24Z"}]},"reasoning":"Measured by the code-factory-perf tick code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-16-08-21 while closing PERF-014. The gate at 400a5ab emitted 34 PASS rows and cost 1.55/1.51/1.49 s user+sys. Commit 77caa02 (CF-075, landed by a sibling lane mid-tick) added section 16 to tests/selftest.sh: six new PASS rows costing, from bash times stamps at 532e7b8, staged disk floor 0.151 s, missing disk floor 0.015 s, manifest validation 0.016 s, owned-failure naming 0.073 s, reused-agent 0.051 s, copy-failure 0.039 s = 0.345 s of a 1.735 s gate. That is three times the 0.09 s cut PERF-014 delivered, and it is the second largest arm in the gate after section 15's 0.524 s of protected documented-command runs. The rows are real assertions, not filler: the question is only whether each needs its own node-create.sh run or can share one staged fixture.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Attribute section 16's six rows individually with a re-runnable script (/usr/bin/time -p, three runs each), not by quoting the foreman's table.\n2. Cut the largest row (staged disk floor resolves, 0.151 s) by a measured amount without losing what it proves: node creation stages every script it executes and resolves the floor from env. Before/after for that arm AND for the whole gate, three consecutive runs each, commands quoted, same tree otherwise.\n3. No assertion dropped, renamed or weakened: the gate keeps 40 PASS rows and SELFTEST: PASS, and the 34 rows present at 400a5ab keep their exact names and counts.\n4. Numbers, comman